  changes: 'Edison LITERATURE (PaperQA3) identity research; report at research/ingredients/Dehydrated_RCM_Medium-edison-literature.md
    (local artifact — research/ is gitignored, so the findings are quoted here rather
    than linked). Report verdict: **Recommended interpretation:** “dehydrated RCM
    medium” denotes the dry preparation of **Reinforced Clostridial Medium (RCM)**,
    a complete, multi-component microbiological growth medium. It is neither a single
    chemical nor a salt, hydrate, buffer, or taxonomic entity. Published recipes contain
    peptone, yeast extract, and beef extract/Lab-Lemco, so the medium is chemically
    complex and incompletely  No ontology CURIE was proposed. Recorded as provenance
    only — no grounding applied from this run. Edison''s recommendations are deliberately
